; DERIVED FROM THE SPRITE ART, NOT LEFT AS THE PLACEHOLDER GRAYS (the Vauban's own SP5 ruling,
; re-run here). Measured 2026-09-19 with the same shader-literal test palette_swap_func.gdshaderinc
; uses (pixel == (v,0,0)/(0,v,0)/(0,0,v)/(0,v,v) for v in palette_index_r.png's seven red values):
; mf_primrose.png (80x80, 2,696 opaque pixels) has ZERO channel-encoded pixels, so this scheme is
; INERT on this sprite exactly like the Vauban's - it cannot repaint the token at all.
; So base_0..2 hold the sprite's OWN most-common literal fill colors (a plain colour census,
; excluding the pure-black linework at 178px/0,0,0): a teal-grey (97px), a pale grey (41px) and a
; muted violet (37px), most-used first per the Iskander's own slot convention. When real
; channel-encoded art replaces this sprite, it inherits a default that already looks like what the
; art shows today, instead of grey.
[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_colorscheme"]
script = ExtResource("3_colorscheme")
base_0 = Color(0.4627451, 0.5372549, 0.56078434, 1)
base_1 = Color(0.654902, 0.7137255, 0.7294118, 1)
base_2 = Color(0.36078432, 0.28235295, 0.38039216, 1)

